{"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"Getting Started with ECS","modules":[{"name":"ECS"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In an entity component system, the things your program tracks are "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"entities","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": plain handles that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own nothing themselves. The data lives in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"components"}]},{"type":"text","text":", small value types attached to entities,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as a position or a health bar. The behavior lives in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"systems","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", functions that run over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every entity holding a particular set of components. A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"world"}]},{"type":"text","text":" holds the entities and their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components, and a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"schedule","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" runs systems on it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This article builds a tiny game step by step: balls that move, and that disappear when their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"health runs out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Define-Components","text":"Define Components","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A component is a value type that conforms to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Component"},{"type":"text","text":". It needs no other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requirements; a struct with stored properties is enough. A component can also be empty, to mark"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the entities that have it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following components describe where an entity is, how fast it moves, and how much health it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Spawn-Entities","text":"Spawn Entities","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World"},{"type":"text","text":" holds entities and their components. Create an empty world, then call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spawn(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" with the components a new entity starts with. Spawning returns an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity"},{"type":"text","text":", the handle you use to read and change that entity later:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","let rock = world.spawn(Position(x: 5, y: 5))","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"2\"","","world[Position.self, of: ball].x = 10","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 10.0, y: 0.0)\"","","world.insert(Health(current: 3), into: rock)","print(world.contains(Health.self, in: rock))","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The subscript reads one component of one entity, and changes it in place when you assign through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert(_:into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to add a component to an entity, ","type":"text"},{"code":"remove(_:from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to take one away,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"despawn(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to remove the entity and all of its components.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world is a value: assigning it to another variable makes an independent copy, and the two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"share their storage until one of them changes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Like an array subscript, the subscript traps if the entity doesn’t hold the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component, or has been despawned. Each such operation has a ","type":"text"},{"code":"checked","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" spelling, such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"world[checked: Position.self, of: ball]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", that throws an error instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important","type":"aside"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Query-and-Update-Many-Entities","text":"Query and Update Many Entities","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A query visits every entity holding a set of component types. Call "},{"code":"query(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with the types,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and iterate over the result; each row holds the entity followed by its components. Narrow a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"query with "},{"code":"with(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"without(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","world.spawn(Position(x: 5, y: 5))","","for (_, position) in world.query(Position.self).without(Velocity.self) {","    print(position)  \/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 5.0, y: 5.0)\"","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To change components across many entities, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"update(_:reading:body:)"},{"type":"text","text":". It visits every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity holding the written type and the read types, and passes the written component "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"along with a row of the others. This is the fastest way to change many entities:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","let rock = world.spawn(Position(x: 5, y: 5))","","world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self) { position, row in","    position.x += row.components.dx","    position.y += row.components.dy","}","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\"","print(world[Position.self, of: rock])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 5.0, y: 5.0)\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rock has no velocity, so the update skips it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Write-Systems","text":"Write Systems","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system is a rule your program applies over and over, such as moving everything that has a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"velocity. Declare one with the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()"},{"type":"text","text":" macro on a type with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types of the method’s parameters say what the system reads and writes:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update"},{"type":"text","text":" writes components, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them, and an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands"},{"type":"text","text":" records spawns and despawns to apply after the system runs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following systems move each entity by its velocity, and despawn each entity whose health has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run out:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}","","@System","struct Reaper {","    func run(_ living: Query<Health>, commands: inout Commands) {","        for (entity, health) in living where health.current <= 0 {","            commands.despawn(entity)","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because a system states what it touches, a schedule knows which systems can run at the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time. Two parameters whose types conflict, such as two updates of the same component, are a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile-time error."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Run-a-Schedule","text":"Run a Schedule","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs systems in the order you write them. Call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to run every system once on a world:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2), Health(current: 3))","let ghost = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Health(current: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Movement()","    Reaper()","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\"","print(world.contains(ghost))","\/\/ Prints \"false\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems that don’t conflict, like these two, run at the same time; the result is always the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same as running them one after another in the order written. To order systems differently, add","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a constraint such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"Reaper().after(Movement.self)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and to skip a system unless a condition","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holds, add ","type":"text"},{"code":"runIf(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Run-a-Simulation","text":"Run a Simulation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A game or simulation runs its systems every frame. A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" owns a world","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and schedules named by label, and you call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/update(elapsed:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" once a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"frame with the time that passed. Systems added to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/fixedUpdate","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" label run once for every fixed timestep of that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time, so they advance at the same rate however long each frame takes:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2), Health(current: 3))","","var simulation = Simulation(world, fixedTimestep: .milliseconds(10))","simulation.add(to: .fixedUpdate) { Movement() }","simulation.add(to: .update) { Reaper() }","","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(30))","print(simulation.world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0, y: 6.0)\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The 30-millisecond frame covers three timesteps, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"Movement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs three times. Because it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moves each entity by its velocity once a run, the velocity here is a distance per timestep. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system that needs the length of a step reads the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/FixedTime"},{"text":" resource, and one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that needs the length of a frame reads ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Time"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Next-Steps","text":"Next Steps","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Learn about the world in depth, including bundles, relations, hierarchies, events and change","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"detection, in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn about system parameters, ordering and system sets in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn about states and the order of a frame in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ecs\/gettingstarted"]}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Define components, spawn entities, and move them with systems that run in a schedule and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"simulation.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS"]]},"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/run(on:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"run"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"on"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"World","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/run(on:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","title":"run(on:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs each system once on a world, running systems that don’t depend on each other at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same time."}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/FixedTime":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/FixedTime","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/fixedtime","title":"FixedTime","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FixedTime"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FixedTime"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A resource holding the fixed timestep of a simulation.","type":"text"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","title":"World","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A collection of entities, the components they hold, and resources."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","type":"topic","title":"System()","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule":{"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule","title":"SimulationModule","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule","role":"collection","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with states that switch systems on and off."}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/fixedUpdate":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/fixedUpdate","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/fixedupdate","title":"fixedUpdate","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fixedUpdate"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScheduleLabel","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The label of the schedule that runs once for each fixed timestep of elapsed time."}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Component":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Component"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Component","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Component"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A type that can be stored as a component of an entity.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/component","title":"Component","type":"topic"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"abstract":[{"text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","type":"topic","title":"Query","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Commands":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Commands"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A buffer of changes to a world, recorded now and applied later in the order they were","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recorded.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/commands","title":"Commands"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Store the state of a game or simulation as entities and components, and read and change it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queries, updates, and commands."}],"title":"WorldModule","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Time":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Time"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Time"}],"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/time","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Time","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource holding the time a simulation has advanced."}],"title":"Time"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","title":"Schedule","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","title":"Simulation","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Simulation","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Simulation","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A world and its schedules by label, advanced one frame at a time.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation/update(elapsed:)":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/update(elapsed:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"update","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"elapsed","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Advances the simulation by one frame.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"update(elapsed:)","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation\/update(elapsed:)"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"type":"topic","title":"Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems"},"doc://ECS/documentation/ECS":{"url":"\/documentation\/ecs","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Build games and simulations from entities, the components they hold, and systems that update","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them in a declared order.","type":"text"}],"title":"ECS"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Entity":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Entity"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A handle that identifies one entity in a world."}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/entity","type":"topic","title":"Entity"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","title":"Update","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it.","type":"text"}]}}}